@inject NavigationManager Nav

@*
    Rendered for any address that matches no route. Installed as a PWA there is no address bar
    and no browser chrome, so a dead-end "nothing here" page leaves the only way out being to
    force-quit the app - which is exactly how a wrong start_url turned into an app that looked
    broken on launch. Sending the user to the main page instead means an unknown address is a
    momentary blip rather than a trap.

    replace: true so the bad address is not left in history: without it, Back lands right back
    on the dead end.
*@

<div style="padding: 24px; text-align: center; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted);">
    Taking you to the main page...
</div>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        Nav.NavigateTo("app", forceLoad: false, replace: true);
    }
}
